B.1.0. {"problem": "The new optional field `previous_commit` is never filled in. `request_delivery` has no `previous_commit` param, the Authoring handoff `deliver_approved_commit` does not pass one, and no action sets it. `Environment.current_commit` is the only record of what was running, and nothing copies it onto the request. Every delivery request will show the field empty, so the change does not meet its goal of showing what was replaced.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, DeliveryRequest.previous_commit, with request_delivery and record_deployment; authoring handoff deliver_approved_commit", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.1.1. {"problem": "Nothing records which commit was replaced at the moment of deployment. `record_deployment` sets only `deployed` and `refusal`, and `Environment.current_commit` is not updated or read. Even if `previous_commit` were populated, nothing keeps `Environment.current_commit` in step with what is deployed, so the value could be stale or wrong.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, record_deployment and Environment.current_commit", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.1.2. {"problem": "The object gained a property, but the domain `version` is still 1 and the composition still pins interface 1. The authoring domain bumps its version on each change, and consumers cannot tell that the shape of DeliveryRequest changed.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml version; toprope-self.composition.yaml members.delivery", "kind": "other"}
B.1.3. {"problem": "The fixtures and scenarios were not updated. R1–R4 have no `previous_commit`, and no scenario checks that a deployment shows the replaced commit. The new field is untested and its behaviour is undeclared.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, world fixtures R1–R4 and scenarios", "kind": "reference"}
B.1.4. {"problem": "The glossary entry for 'delivery request' and the object description say nothing about the replaced commit. The property has no source or rationale, unlike the other declared elements, which cite an interview or record.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, glossary 'delivery request' and DeliveryRequest description", "kind": "reference"}
B.2.0. {"problem": "The new optional field previous_commit is never filled in. request_delivery has no previous_commit param, and the Authoring handoff deliver_approved_commit does not pass one. No action, such as record_build or record_deployment, sets it. No link or lookup connects a DeliveryRequest to its Environment, because links is empty and environment is just a string. Environment.current_commit is also never set by any action. Every request will therefore show an empty previous_commit, and the stated goal of seeing at a glance what was running before is not met.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, object DeliveryRequest.previous_commit (with actions request_delivery and record_deployment, and Environment.current_commit)", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.2.1. {"problem": "The change adds a property to DeliveryRequest, which Authoring's handoff targets at interface 1.x, but the delivery domain stays at version 1. The composition still pins interface 1. No fixture or scenario uses previous_commit, so nothing checks that it works. The glossary entry for 'delivery request' does not mention it. Authoring bumps its version on its own changes, so the unchanged delivery version looks like an oversight.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, version, fixtures, glossary; toprope-self.composition.yaml, members.delivery.interface", "kind": "other"}
B.3.0. {"problem": "The new `previous_commit` property is declared on DeliveryRequest, but nothing ever sets it. `request_delivery` has no `previous_commit` param, so the Authoring handoff `deliver_approved_commit` cannot pass one. No effect in `record_deployment`, `deploy` or `preview` sets it, and `Environment.current_commit` is never read to fill it. The field will always be empty, so the deployer will not see what the request replaced. The change request is not met.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, object DeliveryRequest.previous_commit, with action request_delivery (params and effects), Environment.current_commit, and authoring handoff deliver_approved_commit", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.4.0. {"problem": "The new optional `previous_commit` property on DeliveryRequest is never set, so it will always be empty and the change does not deliver what was asked. `request_delivery` has no `previous_commit` param, and the Authoring handoff `deliver_approved_commit` does not pass one. No action's effects set it either. `record_deployment` records only `deployed` and `refusal`. Nothing reads `Environment.current_commit`, which is the only place the replaced commit is known, and nothing updates it after a deploy. Whoever deploys would see a blank field instead of what was running before.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, object DeliveryRequest.previous_commit; action request_delivery params; action record_deployment effects; authoring handoff deliver_approved_commit", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.4.1. {"problem": "The change only adds a property. It adds no scenario or fixture showing a request with a previous commit. The existing fixtures R1-R4 have no `previous_commit`, so no scenario would catch the field staying unpopulated. The domain `version` stays at 1 even though the object's shape changed.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, world fixtures, scenarios and version", "kind": "other"}
B.5.0. {"problem": "The new optional previous_commit property on DeliveryRequest is never filled in. request_delivery has no previous_commit param, and the authoring handoff deliver_approved_commit does not pass one. No action's effects set it, and no scenario or fixture exercises it. The kernel replies (record_build, record_deployment) don't carry it either. Every request will therefore show an empty previous commit, so the stated goal of seeing what was running before is not met.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, objects.DeliveryRequest.properties.previous_commit; actions.request_delivery / record_deployment", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.5.1. {"problem": "There is nothing to derive the previous commit from. Environment.current_commit is the only record of what is running, and no action ever sets it, not even record_deployment on a successful deploy. DeliveryRequest also has no link to Environment (links is empty, and environment is just a string). Even if previous_commit were wired up, it would have no data to read.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, objects.Environment.current_commit; links: {}; actions.record_deployment", "kind": "other"}
B.5.2. {"problem": "The delivery interface gained a property, but the domain version is still 1. The composition still pins interface 1 and version 1. Changing a declared object without a version bump means the change is not distinguishable from the previously deployed declaration. Authoring bumps its version on change (14).", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml version; toprope-self.composition.yaml members.delivery", "kind": "other"}

